# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Append-only audit log: every lane appends run records, so parallel branches
# collide at EOF on merge. `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' added lines instead
# of raising a conflict (records are independent; order/duplication is tolerable
# for an audit trail). Re-derive a sorted view downstream if ever needed.
#
# The run log is sharded into per-lane files under docs/agent-logs/runs/ (T-046).
# `merge=union` here auto-resolves LOCAL rebase/merge collisions on a shared shard
# (e.g. the dated `*-main.jsonl` lane). NOTE: this is a complement to — not a
# replacement for — the T-046 sharding: GitHub does NOT run merge drivers
# server-side, so sharding remains what prevents server-side PR conflicts; this
# attribute only helps merges/rebases performed locally. The consolidated
# agent-runs.jsonl is a gitignored derived view (T-046), so it needs no attribute.
docs/agent-logs/runs/*.jsonl merge=union

# T-155 — the two INVOLUNTARILY shared append-only files (class 2 in
# docs-eng-process/parallel-lanes.md). Hooks and `/openup-complete-task` step 6
# append to these on every lane's behalf, into fixed paths in the consumer's
# checkout, so no lane can opt out and neither file can be sharded from here.
#
# Inert in THIS repo (it gitignores /.claude/*); they matter only in a project
# that TRACKS .claude/. Evidence from such a project, 2026-07-27: of the merge
# commits touching bypass-log.md, 3 of 3 required reconciling both parents —
# each a LOCAL `merge origin/main into <branch>`, exactly the case a merge
# driver runs for. iteration-learnings.md had 0 (one append per completion,
# and completions are serial); it gets the attribute anyway because it is the
# same shape, and a per-file split would encode "hasn't bitten yet" as design.
#
# NOT a fix, a mitigation — same caveat as the run log above: GitHub does NOT
# run merge drivers server-side, so a PR that conflicts on these files still
# conflicts. Sharding (the T-046 treatment) was considered and rejected: unlike
# agent-runs.jsonl these are read DIRECTLY at a fixed path by an agent at
# session start, so sharding would need a consolidation step nothing runs, in
# the consumer's checkout. See docs/changes/archive/T-155/plan.md.
.claude/memory/bypass-log.md merge=union
.claude/memory/iteration-learnings.md merge=union
